All the comforting flavors of chicken parmesan packed into an easy 30-minute weeknight burger. Ground chicken is seasoned with garlic, herbs, and Parmesan, pan-seared, and finished in simmering marinara under gooey melted mozzarella.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a49120/chicken-parm-burger-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 lb. ground chicken
- ½ cup Italian-style seasoned breadcrumbs
- ¼ cup freshly chopped parsley
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- ¼ cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 1 tablespoon vegetable or olive oil
- 2 cups marinara sauce (plus more for spreading)
- ¾ cup shredded mozzarella cheese
- 4 burger or brioche buns, toasted
- Fresh basil, thinly sliced for garnish

## Instructions

1. **Shape the Seasoned Patties:** In a medium mixing bowl, combine ground chicken, seasoned Italian breadcrumbs, finely chopped parsley, minced garlic, and grated Parmesan cheese. Season generously with kosher salt and freshly cracked black pepper. Use your fingers or a fork to gently blend everything until just cohesive, being careful not to overwork the meat. Shape into 4 burger patties about ½-inch thick.
2. **Sear to a Golden Crust:** Heat 1 tablespoon of cooking oil in a large skillet or sauté pan set over medium-high heat. Lay the patties into the hot pan and let them sear untouched for 4 to 5 minutes until a rich, caramelized crust forms underneath.
3. **Add Marinara and Mozzarella:** Carefully turn each burger patty over. Pour the 2 cups of marinara sauce directly into the skillet, letting it flow around and between the patties. Drop the heat to medium so the tomato sauce simmers gently. Crown each patty with an even layer of shredded mozzarella cheese.
4. **Cover and Braise:** Place a tight lid over the skillet. Allow the burgers to simmer in the sauce for 10 to 12 minutes. The chicken should cook completely to an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C), and the mozzarella will melt into a blanket of bubbling cheese.
5. **Build the Burgers:** Ladle a spoonful of the hot, rich marinara from the pan onto each toasted bottom bun. Transfer a cheesy patty onto each bun, scatter with freshly shredded basil, and top with the toasted bun crowns. Serve warm.

## Notes

- **Moist Chicken Patties:** Italian breadcrumbs and grated Parmesan help bind the lean ground chicken while locking in moisture during cooking.
- **Bun Choice:** Brioche buns, ciabatta rolls, or toasted garlic bread buns make fantastic pairings.
